        "First acknowledge (*I hear you*), then offer a solution. Example: “I hear you. What if we did it during your lunch break?”",
        "“Everybody has time” and “No, it’s not long” argue with the patient. “Your teeth will fall out” scares. “You must find the time” is an order. All of these make people say no.",
        "So: *I hear you. What if we booked it on a Saturday morning?* Tip: listen first, then solve."
