     "text": "TEXT TO A FRIEND (from Claire to Jess)\nUgh, the AC in our apartment died AGAIN 😩 It’s like 90 degrees inside. Can I come work from your place this afternoon? I’ll bring iced coffee lol\n\nEMAIL TO THE PROPERTY MANAGER\nSubject: AC not working, Unit 210\n\nHi Mr. Rivera,\n\nI hope you’re doing well. I wanted to let you know that the AC in Unit 210 stopped working again this morning. This is the second time this month, and the temperature inside is now around 90 degrees.\n\nWould you be able to send someone to take a look today or tomorrow? I’m available all day and can let the technician in. I’ve attached a photo of the thermostat.\n\nThanks so much for your help.\n\nBest,\nClaire Martin\nUnit 210\n\nFORMAL LETTER (two weeks later, after no answer)\nDear Mr. Rivera,\n\nI am writing to follow up on my email of June 3 regarding the air conditioning in Unit 210. Despite two previous requests, the unit has not been repaired, and indoor temperatures have exceeded 88 degrees for twelve consecutive days.\n\nUnder my lease agreement, the landlord is responsible for maintaining the air conditioning system in working condition. I respectfully request that the repair be completed within seven days of this letter.\n\nI would appreciate your prompt attention to this matter. Please contact me at your earliest convenience to confirm a repair date.\n\nSincerely,\nClaire Martin",
