       "why": "An order sounds rude. Make it a question with a cushion: *Could you…?* / *Would you be able to…?*",
       "whyFr": "Un ordre sonne impoli. Fais-en une question avec un coussin : *Could you…?* / *Would you be able to…?*",
       "walk": [
        "The clue: *Give me the schedule.* is an order. You need to turn it into a polite question.",
        "Add a cushion and make it a question: *Could you…?* or *Would you be able to…?* Example: “Could you send me the address, please?”",
        "Just adding *please* (“Give me the schedule, please”) is still an order. “You can give me…?” is missing the question order.",
        "So: *Could you give me the schedule?* (or *send me*) Tip: order → *Could you* + same verb + *?*"
       ],
       "walkFr": "L’indice : *Give me the schedule.* est un ordre. Il faut en faire une question polie. Ajoute un « coussin » et fais une question : *Could you…?* ou *Would you be able to…?* Exemple : « Could you send me the address, please? » Ajouter seulement *please* (« Give me the schedule, please ») reste un ordre. « You can give me…? » n’a pas l’ordre d’une question. Donc : *Could you give me the schedule?* (ou *send me*) Astuce : ordre → *Could you* + même verbe + *?*"
