        "*I’m not a huge fan of…* is an understatement = “I don’t really like it”. Example: “I’m not a huge fan of spicy food.”",
        "“Loves it” is the opposite. “A famous singer” takes *fan* the wrong way. “Never heard it” isn’t said. “A small fan” takes it too literally.",
        "So she *doesn’t really like it*. Tip: a polite way to say no to something without sounding rude."
