        "*It’s not really my thing, but thank you!* says no without judging the activity. Example: “Karaoke’s not really my thing, but have fun!”",
        "“I hate yoga. It’s stupid” insults her hobby. “I don’t like” is missing *it*. “I am not interesting in yoga” is a classic mix-up: *interesting* = « intéressant »; you mean *interested*. “Maybe one day. Never.” is confusing and a bit rude.",
        "So: *It’s not really my thing, but thank you!* Tip: I’m *interested* (me) / it’s *interesting* (the thing)."
