        "*I’m going to pass* = « je vais passer mon tour », a polite no. You need all three: *am* + *going* + *to*. Example: “I’m going to pass on dessert, thanks.”",
        "“I’m go to pass” forgets the *-ing*. “I’m gonna” is how it sounds, but don’t write it. *Will* doesn’t fit after *I’m*.",
        "So: *I’m going to pass this time, but thank you!* Tip: *pass* = « passer son tour » (not « passer » like time)."
