       "walk": [
        "The clue: a *hook* has one job: make people want the rest.",
        "*You will not believe what happened at work today* makes everyone lean in. Example: “Okay, so the weirdest thing happened at the salon…”",
        "The exact date and time is boring. “This is a story” and “I will now tell you a story” are stiff, like a robot. “It’s not very interesting, but…” kills the story before it starts.",
        "So: *You will not believe what happened at work today.* Tip: promise a surprise, then deliver it."
       ],
       "walkFr": "L’indice : une *accroche* n’a qu’un but : donner envie d’entendre la suite. *You will not believe what happened at work today* fait tendre l’oreille à tout le monde. Exemple : « Okay, so the weirdest thing happened at the salon… » La date et l’heure exactes, c’est ennuyeux. « This is a story » et « I will now tell you a story » sont raides, comme un robot. « It’s not very interesting, but… » tue l’histoire avant qu’elle commence. Donc : *You will not believe what happened at work today.* Astuce : promets une surprise, puis donne-la.",
       "p": 0
