        "The background takes *was* + *-ing* (*I was cooking*). The short action in the middle takes the simple past: *came home* (or *got home*). Example: “I was doing my makeup when the doorbell rang.”",
        "“Was coming home” makes both actions long, like they were both in progress; the moment he arrived gets lost. Keep *I was cooking*; it’s already right.",
